# .gcloudignore — prevents non-hub files from uploading to Cloud Run
# The hub/ directory is the deployment unit. Everything else is config/docs.

# Include the default .gitignore behavior
#!include:.gitignore

# Orchestration configs (agent SOULs, KPIs, etc.)
orchestration/

# Scripts (PowerShell/JS admin tools) — but the CSP build gate MUST ship:
# package.json `build` runs scripts/assert-dynamic-rendering.mjs inside the
# container image build, so excluding it breaks `gcloud run deploy` (Cloud
# Build failure 2026-07-14). Uses `scripts/*` rather than `scripts/` because
# gitignore semantics cannot re-include a file whose parent DIRECTORY is
# excluded — only sibling files matched by `*` can be negated back in.
scripts/*
!scripts/assert-dynamic-rendering.mjs

# Memory (local agent memory, untracked)
Memory/

# Railway (legacy migration data)
railway/

# Docs and audit reports — but each skill's SKILL.md is READ AT RUNTIME by
# lib/skills-loader.ts and must ship in the image. The previous negation
# (`!hub/**/*.md`) never matched anything: this ignore file applies INSIDE
# hub/ (the --source dir), where no upload path starts with `hub/`.
*.md
!skills/**/SKILL.md

# Service reference (not used by deploy)
service.yaml

# Git
.git/
.gitignore
